<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-11.00%" pitch="-2.75%">
      But a Samaritan, as he journeyed, came to where the man was.<break time="1000ms"/>
      A Samaritan.<break time="500ms"/>
      To those listening to Jesus, this was a surprising word.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Samaritans and Jews had a long history of division and mutual suspicion.<break time="500ms"/>
      He was the least expected rescuer.<break time="500ms"/>
      The one whose help would have seemed most unlikely to arrive.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And yet he is the one who comes, and stops, and acts.<break time="1800ms"/>

      When he saw him, he had compassion.<break time="500ms"/>
      The same word used for the father who ran to his son.<break time="500ms"/>
      Compassion: a deep, physical movement of the heart toward another person's need.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He did not calculate. He felt, and then he moved.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He went to him.<break time="500ms"/>
      He crossed the road, as the others had crossed to avoid it.<break time="500ms"/>
      He knelt down beside the wounded man.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He bound up his wounds.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He poured on oil and wine.<break time="500ms"/>
      Oil to soothe, wine to clean.<break time="500ms"/>
      He used what he had with him, the things from his own journey.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He gave them freely to someone he had never met.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He set the man on his own animal.<break time="500ms"/>
      He walked so that the wounded man could ride.<break time="500ms"/>
      He brought him to an inn.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And he took care of him through the night.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He stayed.<break time="500ms"/>
      He did not hand him off and hurry on.<break time="500ms"/>
      He stayed and cared for him until morning came.<break time="1800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
